## Context

All eight §2 items from the 2026-06-09 review. Blocked by 0501 because the
cohort counts and accuracy numbers must be re-derived from committed artifacts
before the prose can be fixed.

## What to do (in order)

**2.1 Cohort counts 16/14/12.** One "cohorts" paragraph early in §4:
16 models run → 2 excluded for [X, re-derive from measurements.jsonl] →
14-model analysis cohort → 12 in Figure 4 (DeepSeek lacks quality-taxonomy
panel). Every figure caption names its cohort.

**2.2 Annex B parameter contradictions.** Regenerate the Run-parameters
table from `experiments.toml`. Resolve max_tokens (32768 vs 8192) and
budget_usd (15 vs 10).

**2.3 Wikipedia seeding timeline.** State Wikipedia publication date(s)
for the seeded articles. Compare against each model's training cutoff.
State seeding intent (deliberate instrument or pre-existing outreach).

**2.4 ρ = 0.92 caveat.** In abstract and conclusion add:
"(ρ = 0.92 pooled; within-model signal positive but modest, Annex F)".

**2.5 §5 scope.** In the §5 body, state which quality dimensions were
measured (row F1, coverage, provenance counts) and which are deferred
(Phase C cross-evaluation).

**2.6 Status-vocabulary mismatch.** Add one sentence: "Proposed" (~38%
of reference) has no equivalent in the prompt's controlled vocabulary;
this may mechanically depress status accuracy.

**2.7 Cost-savings claim.** Either: substantiate (author's own hours
compiling the reference is a valid data point) or cut the claim.

**2.8 Novelty claims.** Keep three: benchmark gap, per-row provenance ×
temporality, two-grain credibility/reliability scoring. Demote the other
four to plain observations. Drop the cost–F1 non-monotonicity claim entirely.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Cohort paragraph in §4, all figure captions name their cohort
- [ ] Annex B parameters match experiments.toml
- [ ] Wikipedia seeding date stated; model-cutoff comparison present or
      explicitly scoped
- [ ] ρ caveat in abstract and conclusion
- [ ] §5 scope sentence present
- [ ] Status-vocab mismatch sentence present
- [ ] Cost claim substantiated or cut
- [ ] Exactly three novelty claims; others demoted
- [ ] All numbers re-derived from artifacts (not from review text)
- [ ] `make check` passes
